Z||000000||CW85T-Type||09-05-2000||04:32 PM||||Well, I think I broke my tranny in my 85 SE today.  Coming off the freeway, push in the clutch and it is REAL low. put it in neutral, can't put it in gear.  Slow down some and it clunks into first, let out the clutch and nothing.  try 2nd, nothing, 3rd and 4th are gone too.  I coast into a gas station and park it.  Nothing in reverse either.<P>I'm thinking somthing on the input side of the tranny is broken. There was no slippage on the freeway, no burn clutch smell or smoke.<P>Now my questions. How cheap can a 5spd be purchased to put in the car vs a 4spd? Can a 5spd izusu tranny be put in?  What would I need to swap it in?<P>The car is 100% stock and I plan to keep it stock till this motor goes (2.8v6)<P>Thanks,<P>Chris||||reg||11
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||09-05-2000||09:15 PM||||Not sure if the tranny is broke or how to fix it but...<P>I have the Isuzu tranny in my 88 Coupe with a 2.8V6. If you want to go that route I can help you. The tranny was in all 4 cylinder 85-88 Fieros, and is abundant in boneyards. I picked up an extra one with the shifter, cables, rear calipers, struts and rear suspension pieces from an 88 for $150. <P>The Isuzu will bolt right up to the 2.8 and all you need is:<BR>-the tranny (of course)<BR>-the mounts (they might be useable on the tranny you find)<BR>-a new clutch for the <B>Isuzu</B>, this includes the throw-out bearing and all<BR>-the 5 speed shifter (the 4speed shifter will not work(unless you don't mind not getting into reverse and 5th))<BR>-not sure which master/slave cylinder you have (prolly the first design) they might work and may not. <P><p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 09-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||CW85T-Type||09-07-2000||04:04 AM||||I found a salvage yard that has the tranny's 5spd Izusu for $150 with a 6 month warrenty, so I am going to order it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I plan on going to the bone  yards this w/e to pull the other necesary parts.  Should I pull the master/slave cyl off the "donor car"?  How does the tranny come out? (through the top or do I have to drop the cradle?)  How does the Izusu tranny shift compared to the muncie/getrag?  My 4spd was real notchy and a bit difficult to change gears compared to my old CRX, athough it did give a nice exotick shifting sound going through the gears  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>TIA<BR>Chris<BR>1985 Fiero SE v6 (a white one <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)||||reg||1
